---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/i18n';

export const prerender = true;

Astro.locals.locale = 'en';

const cookiesUrl = href('/cookies', 'en');
const favoritesUrl = href('/favoritos', 'en');
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" updated="August 2026">
  <p>
    At Madrid Movilidad (madmovil.es) we process as little data as possible: we use no advertising, no
    analytics, no trackers and no profiling, and we never share your data with third parties for commercial
    purposes. This policy explains, in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Spanish Organic Law
    3/2018 (LOPDGDD), what data we process, for what purpose and what rights you have.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controller:</strong> the owner of Madrid Movilidad (a private individual, with no business activity)</li>
    <li><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:info@madmovil.es">info@madmovil.es</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What data we process and why</h2>

  <h3>2.1. Anonymous use</h3>
  <p>
    We do not process any personal data. Your favourite stops and preferences (for example, the light or dark
    theme) are stored solely in your browser’s local storage (<em>localStorage</em>) and never leave your
    device. You can delete them at any time from your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h3>2.2. Favourites sync across devices (optional)</h3>
  <p>
    If you enable it, your favourites are <strong>encrypted on your own device</strong> (AES-GCM-256, Web
    Crypto) and our servers only store the encrypted content, identified by a value derived irreversibly from
    your sync code. Neither the code nor the encryption key ever leaves your devices: we cannot decrypt or
    read your favourites. <em>Purpose:</em> letting you take your favourites to other devices. <em>Legal basis:</em> performance
    of a contract for the provision of the service (Art. 6.1.b GDPR). The
    encrypted copy is automatically deleted after 180 days without synchronisation, and you can delete it at
    any time (“Delete remote copy” on the Favourites page).
  </p>

  <h3>2.3. Technical data</h3>
  <p>
    As with any web service, the network infrastructure automatically and temporarily processes your IP address
    and basic request data in order to route traffic, prevent abuse and limit excessive requests. <em>Purpose:</em> security
    and availability of the service. <em>Legal basis:</em> legitimate interest
    (Art. 6.1.f GDPR). They are kept only for as long as strictly necessary for those purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising, analytics and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    We use no cookies or equivalent technologies for analytics, advertising, audience measurement or profiling,
    and we do not share data with advertising networks. You can see the details in the <a href={cookiesUrl}>cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or share your personal data with third parties. To operate the service we use:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.:</strong> hosting and delivery of the site and its API (Workers and CDN),
      including the encrypted favourites sync copy and the anti-abuse check when setting up sync (Turnstile).
      It acts as a data processor. This may involve a transfer of data to the United States, covered by the
      EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may disclose data to public authorities only where required by a legal obligation (Art. 6.1.c GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Favourites and preferences in your browser: until you delete them from the site or your browser.</li>
    <li>Sync copy (encrypted): up to 180 days without synchronisation, or until you delete it (“Delete remote copy”).</li>
    <li>Technical data: short retention periods limited to the security purpose described above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Your rights and how to exercise them</h2>
  <p>
    You can exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing and
    portability, as well as withdraw consent where applicable, by writing to <a href="mailto:info@madmovil.es">info@madmovil.es</a> with
    sufficient information to verify your identity.
    We will respond within one month at the latest. You may also lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data
    Protection Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">aepd.es</a>) if
    you believe your rights have been infringed.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    You can do it yourself, without writing to us: local favourites and preferences are managed and deleted
    from the <a href={favoritesUrl}>Favourites</a> page or from your browser, and the remote sync copy is
    removed with the <strong>“Delete remote copy”</strong> button (immediately and irreversibly). As an
    alternative, you can request deletion by email.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Minors</h2>
  <p>
    This service is not directed at children under 14. Under Article 7 of the LOPDGDD, processing the data of
    children under 14 requires the consent of their parents or legal guardians.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy to adapt it to legal changes or changes in the service. Any modification will be
    published on this same page, indicating the date of the last update.
  </p>
</Legal>
